<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Bush returns eight weeks after starting levothyroxine 75 mcg daily. His tiredness and constipation are better, and he feels cold only occasionally. He took metoprolol 25 mg daily for eight weeks and finished the taper this week. He wore the 14-day ECG patch for the two weeks ending four days ago, with no palpitations. He takes apixaban twice daily with no bleeding. He runs three miles four days a week without symptoms and has regained his usual weight. He takes levothyroxine alone on an empty stomach each morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Thyroid symptoms</td><td>Tiredness and constipation better; occasionally cold</td></tr><tr><td>Rhythm</td><td>No palpitations; 14-day patch completed</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Levothyroxine 75 mcg daily; metoprolol taper completed; apixaban twice daily</td></tr><tr><td>Activity</td><td>Running three miles four days a week</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

